// LOW cohesion + HIGH coupling: one class touches everything (bad)
class BadModule {
    void saveUser(Object u) { /* db */ }
    void sendEmail(String t) { /* smtp */ }
    double calcTax(double a) { return a * 0.18; } // unrelated concerns lumped together
}

// HIGH cohesion + LOW coupling: focused class depending on an abstraction
interface TaxCalculator { double calculate(double amount); }

class OrderService {                      // cohesive: only order logic
    private final TaxCalculator tax;      // loose: depends on an interface
    OrderService(TaxCalculator tax) { this.tax = tax; }
    double total(double subtotal) { return subtotal + tax.calculate(subtotal); }
}
```
The goal is to push cohesion up and coupling down at the same time.

